ndId":372,"limited":371,"fileSize":373,"isPublic":374,"original":375,"copyright":19,"extension":376,"thumbnails":378,"dateCreated":386,"description":387,"orientation":388,"userCreated":389,"watermarked":371,"dateModified":386,"datePublished":390,"ecsArchiveFiles":391,"propertyOptions":392,"property_Channel":397,"property_Sub-Type":399,"property_Asset_Type":401,"activeOriginalFocusPoint":403,"property_Office_Department":406},"DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/webimage-292A98B4-C2DA-4255-8154333AF5EC4511.png","FHORT_Main Visual_Green_Website",[319,320,321,322,323,324,325,326,327,328,329,330,331,332,333,334,335,336,337,338,339,340,341,342,343,344,345,346,347,348,349,350,351,352,353,354,355,356,357,358,359,360,361,362,363,127,364,365,366],"built structure","vegetable garden","summer","plant nursery","plant","flower","technology","freshness","environment","agriculture","factory","outdoors","metal","environmental conservation","vegetable","architecture","day","station","leaf","blue","industry","people","springtime","botany","garden center","backgrounds","indoors","biology","food","nature","cultures","gardening","steel","green color","men","growth","in a row","modern","equipment","organic","inside of","cultivated","business","seedling","farm","color image","greenhouse","glass - material","image",6720,4480,"6bdc76db503fe1d7",0,"22C10171-81B3-4DA6-99342F272A32E8BB",27961258,1,"https://brand.frontiersin.org/m/6bdc76db503fe1d7/original/FHORT_Main-Visual_Green_Website.jpg",[377],"jpg",{"mini":379,"thul":380,"webimage":316,"Guidelines":381,"WebsiteJpg_XL":382,"WebsiteWebP_L":383,"WebsiteWebP_M":384,"WebsiteWebP_XL":385},"https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/mini-55C9A04A-43DA-4267-910FEA646411FEAF.png","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/thul-2BD02E36-4890-4B28-9598EC1FA7B43F5D.png","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/3B51817D-6A57-4F74-93B6B3F452CC0D9C/Guidelines-FHORT_Main Visual_Green_Website.png","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/3B51817D-6A57-4F74-93B6B3F452CC0D9C/WebsiteJpg_XL-FHORT_Main Visual_Green_Website.jpg","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/3B51817D-6A57-4F74-93B6B3F452CC0D9C/WebsiteWebP_L-FHORT_Main Visual_Green_Website.webp","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/3B51817D-6A57-4F74-93B6B3F452CC0D9C/WebsiteWebP_M-FHORT_Main Visual_Green_Website.webp","https://d2csxpduxe849s.cloudfront.net/media/E32629C6-9347-4F84-81FEAEF7BFA342B3/DF7BD750-14DB-4110-BDB43F5BB39480B6/3B51817D-6A57-4F74-93B6B3F452CC0D9C/WebsiteWebP_XL-FHORT_Main Visual_Green_Website.webp","2022-06-27T09:59:51Z","Botanist in white lab coat working with plants in the greenhouse; Shutterstock ID 1668575008; purchase_order:Corporate library; job:; client:; other:","landscape","Caroline Sutter","2022-06-27T09:27:09Z",[],[393,394,395,396],"414FB2D4-2283-43FD-BE14E534ECA67928","6C18119B-14BD-4951-B437696F4357BD33","7C692885-DB25-4858-B1FB4FF47B241E9B","D88C0047-EC30-4506-A7DF28A4D765E1CF",[398],"frontiersin_org",[400],"Main_Visual",[402],"Photography",{"x":404,"y":405},3360,2240,[407],"Publishing","Explore open‑access research in horticulture with studies on crops, plant health, soils, production systems and sustainability.","\u003Cp>Frontiers in Horticulture is a multidisciplinary journal that publishes fundamental and applied research on all horticultural crops, including pulse crops, vegetables, fruits, herbs, tea, flowers, and ornamental trees.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Led by Field Chief Editor Prof Xiangming Xu (National Institute of Agricultural Botany [NIAB], UK) and indexed in the DOAJ, the journal welcomes studies that advance our understanding of horticultural crops to benefit growers and consumers, as well as on the implementation and evaluation of research solutions in commercial horticulture. Topics of interest include, but are not limited to:\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cul>\n  \u003Cli>application of the ‘microbiome’ concept to improve plant and soil health\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>application of ‘-omics’ in horticultural crops\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>genetics and breeding\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>precision agronomy and improving resource use efficiency\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>post-harvest processing and management\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>substrate and soil health for improving and maintaining crop productivity\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>sustainable pest and disease management\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>the role of commercial horticulture in landscape management\u003C/li>\n  \u003Cli>waste reduction and re-purposing.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\n\u003Cp>The journal particularly welcomes submissions with broad international and interdisciplinary interest and which advance the UN’s Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), notably SDG 2: zero hunger; SDG 12; responsible consumption and production; and SDG 15: life on land.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Research studies with an emphasis on social science, such as human health benefits associated with fruit and vegetable consumption, are not suitable for publication in this journal.\u003C/p>\n\n\u003Cp>Frontiers in Horticulture is committed to advancing horticultural sciences by communicating scientific knowledge to researchers and the public alike, to enable the scientific breakthroughs of the future.\u003C/p>","green","nan","702",{"id":125,"name":126,"slug":127,"abbreviation":414,"isOnline":13,"isOpenForSubmissions":-1,"impactFactor":415,"citeScore":416},"fhort",3,3.3,{"displayTitlePillLabels":13,"displayRelatedArticlesBox":13,"showEditors":13,"showReviewers":13,"showLoopImpactLink":13,"enableFigshare":310},{"isPublic":310,"allowCompanyUsers":310,"whiteListEmails":419,"enableAllJournals":310,"whiteListJournals":420},[],[],{"spaceId":374,"name":374,"availableJournalPages":422,"announcement":426,"useJournalPalettes":310},[217,222,219,423,424,425],"volumes","about","community-reviewers",{"__typename":427,"sys":428,"preHeader":430,"title":431,"description":432,"image":433,"link":506},"Announcement",{"id":429},"30jAeTjZfu9FwrF5jqYs9f","Our quality","Expert judgment makes science stronger"," Behind every published article stand expert reviewers safeguarding science. Discover our rigorous approach to peer review.",[434],{"id":435,"src":436,"name":437,"tags":438,"type":367,"width":487,"height":488,"archive":371,"brandId":372,"limited":371,"fileSize":489,"isPublic":374,"original":490,"copyright":28,"extension":491,"thumbnails":492,"dateCreated":500,"description":437,"orientation":388,"watermarked":371,"dateModified":501,"selectedFile":28,"datePublished":502,"streamingLinks":503,"videoPreviewURLs":504,"textMetaproperties":505},"E8101B5E-CD70-402C-B234D8C42CD1D053","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/thumbnail/webimage-Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass","Doctor making notes in hospital, corona virus concept. Shot through glass.",[439,440,441,442,443,444,445,446,447,448,449,450,451,452,453,454,455,456,457,458,459,460,461,462,463,464,465,466,467,468,469,470,471,472,473,474,475,353,476,477,478,479,480,481,482,483,484,485,486],"global","professional","pandemic","conference","contagious","pneumonia","respiratory","medical","glass","exhausted","outbreak","corona","virus","making notes","writing","DOCTOR","contamination","training","Risk","Coronavirus","Science","warning","Hospital","health","close-up","infection","research","safety","prevention","concept","danger","Indoors","Disease","fever","scientist","flu","protection","viral","copy space","shot","Clinic","illness","healthcare","cure","seminar","epidemic","treatment","working on",4928,3280,14062390,"https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.jpg",[377],{"mini":493,"thul":494,"original":490,"webimage":436,"Guidelines":495,"WebsiteJpg_XL":496,"WebsiteWebP_L":497,"WebsiteWebP_M":498,"WebsiteWebP_XL":499},"https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/thumbnail/mini-Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/thumbnail/thul-Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/Guidelines/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.png","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteJpg_XL/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.jpg","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteWebP_L/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.webp","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteWebP_M/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.webp","https://brand.frontiersin.org/asset/e8101b5e-cd70-402c-b234-d8c42cd1d053/WebsiteWebP_XL/Doctor-making-notes-in-hospital-corona-virus-concept-Shot-through-glass.webp","2022-05-10T11:52:42Z","2026-02-11T15:34:30Z","2022-05-11T12:46:58Z",{},[],[],{"text":507,"url":67,"target":27,"ariaLabel":28},"Learn about peer review",{"loggedUserInfo":-1},{"currentArticle":510,"isPreviewPage":310,"hasSupplementalData":310,"showCrossmarkWidget":13,"articleTemplate":693,"currentArticlePageMetaInfo":694,"xmlParsedArticleContent":852,"xmlParsingError":-1},{"id":511,"doi":512,"title":513,"acceptanceDate":514,"receptionDate":515,"publicationDate":516,"lastModifiedDate":517,"isPublished":13,"abstract":518,"researchTopic":519,"articleType":525,"stage":528,"keywords":530,"authors":538,"editors":625,"reviewers":635,"journal":653,"section":660,"impactMetrics":662,"volume":415,"articleVolume":666,"relatedArticles":667,"isPublishedV2":310,"contents":668,"laySummary":19,"files":669},1425366,"10.3389/fhort.2024.1425366","New insights in the flavor and chemistry of Huanglongbing tolerant citrus hybrids with/without Poncirus trifoliata in their pedigree",["Date","2024-08-16T08:18:09.000Z"],["Date","2024-04-29T16:01:21.000Z"],["Date","2024-09-10T00:00:00.000Z"],["Date","2026-09-22T02:07:26.886Z"],"Citrus hybrids with Poncirus trifoliata L. Raf. introgression have gained interest due to their tolerance to Huanglongbing (HLB), a devastating disease for Florida citrus agriculture. While these hybrids inherit disease tolerance from P. trifoliata, they sometimes also suffer from undesirable offflavors. A selection of thirteen genotypes were harvested over the 2020-2021 and 2021-2022 seasons. Their juices were evaluated by a trained sensory panel and were comprehensively analyzed for their chemical makeup, including soluble solids content (SSC), titratable acidity (TA), volatiles, flavonoids and limonoids. Overall, along with the commercial orange cultivars 'Valencia' and 'Hamlin', the HLB-tolerant Poncirus hybrid 'US SunDragon,' and the mandarin hybrids Sugar Belle ® , FF-5-51-2, and 'US Superna' had positive citrus flavor quality. Esters, some sesquiterpenes, along with flavonoids, eriocitrin and quercetin-3-(3R-glucosylrutinoside), were positively correlated with orange flavor while β-ionone and eucalyptol were highly abundant in the mandarins. The flavonoid linarin, was more abundant in Poncirus hybrids with off-flavors than in the Poncirus hybrid 'US SunDragon', having high orange flavor. Two mandarin hybrids, FF-5-6-36 and FTP-6- 32-67, were not bitter at harvest, but the juice exhibited delayed bitterness after storage at -20 °C, which was associated with significant increases of limonin, nomilin, naringenin, and prunin. Interestingly, during freezer storage, a newly identified flavonoid in citrus, tricin-C-hexoside, increased dramatically across all of the genotypes. The identification of disease-tolerant hybrids with satisfactory flavor quality at juicing as well as after storage where delayed bitterness may develop, has great significance for future breeding efforts for fresh fruit or for use in stand-alone juice/juice blends.",{"id":520,"title":521,"articlesCount":522,"isMagazinePage":310,"slug":523,"isOpenForSubmission":310,"views":524},57588,"Citriculture: Sustaining Quality Production",5,"citriculture-sustaining-quality-production",24958,{"id":526,"name":527},24,"Original Research",{"id":529,"name":19},18,[531,532,533,534,535,536,537],"Citrus ×P. trifoliata","Juice flavor","Flavonoids","LC-MS/MS","GC-MS","sensory","HLB",[539,548,556,564,571,578,584,590,596,602,610,618],{"id":540,"firstName":541,"middleName":19,"lastName":542,"givenNames":543,"isCorresponding":310,"isProfilePublic":13,"userId":540,"email":-1,"affiliations":544},2806915,"Kristen A.","Jeffries","Kristen A. ",[545],{"organizationName":546,"countryName":547,"cityName":19,"stateName":19,"zipCode":19},"US Horticultural Research Laboratory, US Department of Agriculture - Agricultural Research Service (USDA-ARS)","United States",{"id":549,"firstName":550,"middleName":19,"lastName":551,"givenNames":552,"isCorresponding":310,"isProfilePublic":13,"userId":549,"email":-1,"affiliations":553},1052732,"Zhen","Fan","Zhen ",[554],{"organizationName":555,"countryName":547,"cityName":19,"stateName":19,"zipCode":19},"Institute of Food and Agricultural Sciences (IFAS) Gulf Coast Research and Education Center, University of Florida, Horticultural Sciences Department",{"id":557,"firstName":558,"middleName":19,"lastName":559,"givenNames":560,"isCorresponding":310,"isProfilePublic":13,